    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with a potent core, anchored by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (77.82) and **Luis Robert Jr.** (75.66). **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** benefits from a favorable matchup against the southpaw Patrick Sandoval, utilizing a 7% platoon bump to secure the highest efficiency score in the lineup. Similarly, **Luis Robert Jr.** is primed for a massive outing against Mart\u00edn P\u00e9rez; his 13% SP skill bonus and 14% platoon advantage make him an essential start. **Gunnar Henderson** remains a focal point for our offense, boasting an 83.29 rating driven by an elite combination of a high-ceiling matchup against Bailey Ober and a 10% order bonus for his spot atop the lineup. **Jacob Wilson** (72.73) and **Kyle Tucker** (71.02) round out our top-tier plays, both benefiting from soft matchups that raise their daily floors significantly.\n\nTactical optimization favored high-upside bats over marginal efficiency, leaving **Nasim Nunez** as the most difficult omission. Despite his speed profile\u2014which we typically overweigh\u2014his 48.11 score fell just short due to a suboptimal spot in the order and a challenging matchup against the craftier Shota Imanaga. We also note that several players, including **Liam Hicks**, **Drake Baldwin**, **Coby Mayo**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Andy Pages**, **Sam Antonacci**, and **Heliot Ramos**, currently carry a \"Lineup Pending\" status. While our model assumes their historical batting positions, we must monitor official lineups closely, particularly for **Heliot Ramos**, whose marginal 52.06 score could drop further if he slides down in the order against Bryan Woo. We are comfortable with our bench depth, including **Curtis Mead**, **Josh Jung**, and **Jackson Merrill**, should any late-scratch contingencies arise, but for now, we remain committed to maximizing our Roto categories through these optimized positional starts.",
